= Erzberger is murdered!

On 26 August Matthias Erzberger of the Centre, who signed the armistice at Compiègne, is shot dead while out walking at Bad Griesbach. His killers are two former naval officers of the Organisation Consul. They escape to Hungary, and part of the nationalist press says openly that he had it coming.

On 31 August hundreds of thousands march against the murderers in the cities of the Reich.

- @march: March with the SPD, the USPD and the unions.
- @defence: Form workers' defence squads in Berlin and the Ruhr.

@march
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Our banners in the same columns as the SPD's. Radek and Lenin will like it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids marching with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.spd_relation += 6;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.comply(15);
!}

In Berlin, Leipzig and Chemnitz the speakers on the platform belong to three parties. The Lustgarten is full from end to end.

@defence
subtitle: Fighting men in two districts, and more police in both.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {guards: 1.5, repression: 5});
RG.district('ruhr', {guards: 1.5, repression: 5});
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

Factory defence squads are formed in Berlin and the Ruhr. They drill in the yards after the shift, with sticks for rifles.
